<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal" dir=3D=
"ltr"><strong>One-sentence explanation:</strong> A console application that=
 lets a user add, view, list, search, edit, and delete contacts (Full Name,=
 Phone, Email), storing them durably in a local JSON file.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal" dir=3D=
"ltr"><strong>Beginner explanation:</strong> Think of it as a digital addre=
ss book you operate entirely by typing numbers and text into a terminal. Yo=
u pick an option from a menu (like "Add Contact"), answer a few prompts, an=
d the program either confirms success or tells you clearly what went wrong =
(like a duplicate phone number). Every change is saved to a file immediatel=
y, so closing and reopening the program never loses your contacts.</p>
<p class=3D"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal" dir=3D=
"ltr"><strong>Technical explanation:</strong> A .NET 8 console application =
layered into Models / Validation / Persistence / Services / UI, where <code=
 class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000=
 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">ContactServ=
ice</code> owns all business rules (CRUD, duplicate policy, search), <code =
class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 =
whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">IContactRepo=
sitory</code>/<code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-=
300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0=
.9rem]">JsonContactRepository</code> isolate storage behind an abstraction,=
 <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-dang=
er-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">Conta=
ctValidator</code> handles input validation and normalization, and <code cl=
ass=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 wh=
itespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">ConsoleMenu</c=
ode> is a thin UI layer with no business logic of its own. Data is persiste=
d as an indented, camelCase JSON array using <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 b=
order border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap roun=
ded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">System.Text.Json</code>, written via=
 a temp-file-then-replace strategy for crash safety.</p>
